<!doctype html><html><head><meta charset="utf-8"><title>Agent 1 report: {{ name }}</title><style>{{ css|safe }}</style></head><body>
{% set s = profile.statistics %}{% set d = decisions %}{% set sp = size_plan %}
<header class="title">
<p class="kicker">BIOS 774 · Agent 1 · evidence-driven dimensionality reduction</p>
<h1>{{ profile.provenance.source|default('Synthetic numerical demonstration') }}</h1>
<p class="meta">Dataset <strong>{{ name }}</strong> · run {{ manifest.created_at[:10] }} · job {{ manifest.job_id }} · commit {{ (manifest.git_commit or 'none')[:10] }}</p>
</header>
<p class="notice">Reporting mode: {{ mode }}. {% if mode == 'deterministic' %}This report was rendered from saved, validated evidence by deterministic templates; no language model wrote it. Every number below is read from a checksummed artifact in the evidence bundle.{% else %}An OpenAI model organized an extractive summary; every returned sentence was checked against the evidence list.{% endif %}</p>

<h2>At a glance</h2>
<table class="kv"><tbody>
<tr><th>Source</th><td>{{ '{:,}'.format(profile.n_samples) }} observations × {{ '{:,}'.format(profile.n_features) }} numerical features{% if cohort.selected < profile.n_samples %}; <strong>the final analysis uses a declared subset ({{ '{:,}'.format(cohort.selected) }} observations), not the complete dataset</strong>{% endif %}</td></tr>
<tr><th>Preprocessing branch</th><td>{{ plan.branch|replace('_', ' ') }} (chosen from the data profile, not the dataset name)</td></tr>
<tr><th>Pilot</th><td>{{ '{:,}'.format(pilot_cohort.selected) }} observations; all ten methods; {{ cfg.pilot.n_repeats_stochastic }} seeds for stochastic methods; {{ cfg.pilot.n_subsamples }} refits on {{ (100 * cfg.pilot.subsample_fraction)|round|int }}% subsamples for every method</td></tr>
<tr><th>Retained</th><td>{% for m in d.selected %}{{ names[m] }}{% if not loop.last %}, {% endif %}{% endfor %}{% if d.low_confidence %} (low-confidence fallback){% endif %}</td></tr>
<tr><th>Final cohort</th><td>{{ '{:,}'.format(cohort.selected) }} observations; binding constraint: {{ sp.binding_constraint }}</td></tr>
</tbody></table>
<h3>Findings</h3>
<ul class="facts">{% for f in facts %}<li>{{ f }}</li>{% endfor %}</ul>
{% if summary %}<h3>API-organized validated evidence</h3>{% for sentence in summary.sentences %}<p>{{ sentence }}</p>{% endfor %}{% endif %}

<h2>1 · Dataset inspection</h2>
<table class="kv"><tbody>
<tr><th>Storage</th><td>{{ s.dtype }}; sparsity {{ '%.4f'|format(s.sparsity) }}; values in [{{ s.min_value|fmt }}, {{ s.max_value|fmt }}]; non-negative: {{ s.nonnegative }}; integer-valued: {{ s.integer_valued }}</td></tr>
<tr><th>Features</th><td>{{ s.constant_features }} constant, {{ s.duplicate_features }} duplicated; feature variance min/median/max {{ s.feature_variance_quantiles|fmt }}; mitochondrial (MT-) features: {{ s.mitochondrial_features }}</td></tr>
<tr><th>Observation totals</th><td>row sums min/median/max {{ s.row_sum_quantiles|fmt }}</td></tr>
<tr><th>Memory</th><td>dense float64 {{ '%.0f'|format(s.dense_float64_mb) }} MB; full pairwise matrix {{ '%.0f'|format(s.pairwise_float64_mb) }} MB (never materialized by the evaluation code)</td></tr>
<tr><th>Secondary labels</th><td>{% for k, v in s.label_counts.items() %}{{ k }} {{ '{:,}'.format(v) }}{% if not loop.last %} · {% endif %}{% endfor %}</td></tr>
</tbody></table>
<p class="small">Labels only stratify cohort composition and color secondary plots. They never enter preprocessing fits, embeddings or selection.</p>

<h2>2 · Preprocessing plan and rationale</h2>
<p>Rule evidence: sparsity {{ '%.3f'|format(plan.rule_evidence.sparsity) }}, non-negative {{ plan.rule_evidence.nonnegative }}, integer-valued {{ plan.rule_evidence.integer_valued }}, {{ '{:,}'.format(plan.rule_evidence.n_features) }} features → branch <strong>{{ plan.branch|replace('_', ' ') }}</strong>. The same plan is re-fitted inside each cohort (pilot and final).</p>
<table><thead><tr><th>Step</th><th>Parameters (final cohort)</th><th>Reason</th><th>Fit scope</th></tr></thead><tbody>
{% for a in plan.actions %}<tr><td>{{ a.action|replace('_', ' ') }}</td><td class="small">{{ a.parameters|params }}</td><td>{{ a.reason }}</td><td>{{ a.fit_scope }}</td></tr>{% endfor %}
</tbody></table>

<h2>3 · Comparable pilot design</h2>
<p>Every method was fitted to the identical saved input ({{ '{:,}'.format(pilot_cohort.input_shape[0]) }} × {{ pilot_cohort.input_shape[1] }}; SHA-256 {{ pilot_cohort.input_sha256[:12] }}…). Stochastic methods (MDS, GPLVM, t-SNE, UMAP) use {{ cfg.pilot.n_repeats_stochastic }} seeds. Every method is also refitted on the same {{ cfg.pilot.n_subsamples }} random {{ (100 * cfg.pilot.subsample_fraction)|round|int }}% subsamples. Metrics use Euclidean distance in the common input space:</p>
<ul class="small">
<li><strong>T</strong>: trustworthiness at k = {{ cfg.pilot.n_neighbors_eval }} (scikit-learn definition).</li>
<li><strong>R</strong>: mean k-nearest-neighbor recall, self excluded, stable tie order.</li>
<li><strong>G</strong>: Spearman correlation of pairwise distances (all pairs up to 500,000, otherwise a fixed random sample), clipped at 0.</li>
<li><strong>S</strong>: mean kNN overlap of subsample refits on their shared observations.</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Quality Q = {{ d.quality_formula|replace('*', ' ')|replace('_', ' ') }}</strong>. The weights and all thresholds were fixed before the real-data run (docs/METHOD_NOTES.md). Runtime is fit_transform time only; imports and JIT warm-up are recorded separately.</p>
<p>Severe diagnostics make a method ineligible: disconnected-graph or singular warnings; a collapsed layout (median collapse ratio &lt; {{ cfg.selection.collapse_absolute }} and &lt; {{ cfg.selection.collapse_relative }} × PCA's); a diffusion Markov spectral gap &lt; {{ '%.0e'|format(cfg.selection.spectral_gap_min) }}; SMACOF reaching max_iter.</p>

<h2>4 · Pilot results</h2>
<table><thead><tr><th>Method</th><th>Status</th><th>T</th><th>R</th><th>G</th><th>S</th><th>Seed S</th><th>Q</th><th>Fit s</th><th>Collapse</th><th>Flags</th></tr></thead><tbody>
{% for r in pilot %}<tr class="{{ 'retained' if r.method in d.selected else '' }}"><td>{{ names[r.method] }}</td><td>{{ r.status }}</td>{% for key in ['trustworthiness','neighbor_recall','global_structure','stability','seed_stability','quality'] %}<td>{{ '%.3f'|format(r[key]) if r[key] is not none else '–' }}</td>{% endfor %}<td>{{ '%.2f'|format(r.runtime_seconds) }}</td><td>{{ '%.2f'|format(r.collapse_ratio) if r.collapse_ratio is not none else '–' }}</td><td class="small">{{ r.severe_reasons|join('; ') if r.severe_reasons else ('seed-invariant' if r.seed_invariant else '') }}</td></tr>{% endfor %}
</tbody></table>
<p class="small">Highlighted rows were retained. Fit s is the mean fit_transform wall time on the full pilot cohort. Seed S is the overlap between repeated seeds on the same cohort; it is shown for stochastic methods only.</p>
{% for key in ['pilot_embeddings', 'pilot_metrics', 'runtime_quality', 'stability'] %}{% set f = figures[key] %}<figure><img src="{{ f.path }}"><figcaption>{{ f.caption }}</figcaption></figure>{% endfor %}

<h2>5 · Evidence-based selection</h2>
<p>Best valid pilot quality is {{ '%.4f'|format(d.best_quality) }} ({{ names[d.best_method] }}); the 90% threshold is {{ '%.4f'|format(d.threshold) }}.</p>
<p>A method is eligible if it meets that threshold, lies within the practical-equivalence margin of the best, or sits on the ε-Pareto frontier. The margin is max(2 × paired subsample SE, {{ cfg.selection.equivalence_floor }}). On the ε-Pareto frontier, a runtime difference counts only when it is ≥ {{ cfg.selection.runtime_material_ratio|fmt }}× and ≥ {{ cfg.selection.runtime_material_seconds|fmt }} s.</p>
<p>PCA is retained as the linear baseline, with at most {{ cfg.selection.max_final_methods }} candidates in total.</p>
<table><thead><tr><th>Method</th><th>Prior (not evidence)</th><th>Decision</th><th>Measured reason</th></tr></thead><tbody>
{% for x in d.decisions %}<tr class="{{ 'retained' if x.decision == 'retain' else '' }}"><td>{{ names[x.method] }}</td><td class="small">{{ x.prior_suitability }}</td><td>{{ x.decision }}</td><td class="small">{{ x.reason }}</td></tr>{% endfor %}
</tbody></table>
<h3>Robustness of the shortlist</h3>
<p>Each row below re-runs the same selection mechanics under one rule change on the same saved evidence; only the first row determined the analysis.</p>
<table><thead><tr><th>Rule variant</th><th>Shortlist</th></tr></thead><tbody>
{% for v in d.sensitivity.variants %}<tr><td>{{ v.variant }}</td><td>{% for m in v.selected %}{{ names[m] }}{% if not loop.last %}, {% endif %}{% endfor %}</td></tr>{% endfor %}
</tbody></table>
<p class="small">Selection frequency across variants: {% for m, f in d.sensitivity.selection_frequency.items() %}{{ names[m] }} {{ (100 * f)|round|int }}%{% if not loop.last %} · {% endif %}{% endfor %}.</p>
<h3>From the v1 rules to the pre-registered v2 rules</h3>
<p>This cumulative ablation is computed on the same evidence; each step changes one rule.</p>
<table><thead><tr><th>Step</th><th>Shortlist</th></tr></thead><tbody>
{% for a in d.ablation %}<tr><td>{{ a.step }}</td><td>{% for m in a.selected %}{{ names[m] }}{% if not loop.last %}, {% endif %}{% endfor %}</td></tr>{% endfor %}
</tbody></table>
{% set f = figures['sensitivity'] %}<figure><img src="{{ f.path }}" class="narrow"><figcaption>{{ f.caption }}</figcaption></figure>

<h2>6 · Shortlist refinement</h2>
<p>Only retained methods were tuned. Each grid point was evaluated with the same seeds, subsamples and quality as the pilot. A non-default point replaces the default only if it gains more than the paired equivalence margin.</p>
<table><thead><tr><th>Method</th><th>Grid</th><th>Changed parameters</th><th>Status</th><th>Q</th><th>S</th><th>Fit s</th></tr></thead><tbody>
{% for r in tuning %}<tr class="{{ 'retained' if tuning_decisions[r.method].grid_index == r.grid_index else '' }}"><td>{{ names[r.method] }}</td><td>{{ r.grid_index }}</td><td class="small">{{ r.changed|params if r.changed else 'default' }}</td><td>{{ r.status }}{% if r.severe_reasons %} (severe){% endif %}</td><td>{{ '%.3f'|format(r.quality) if r.quality is not none else '–' }}</td><td>{{ '%.3f'|format(r.stability) if r.stability is not none else '–' }}</td><td>{{ '%.2f'|format(r.runtime_seconds) }}</td></tr>{% endfor %}
</tbody></table>
<ul class="small">{% for m, x in tuning_decisions.items() %}<li><strong>{{ names[m] }}</strong>: {{ x.reason }}.</li>{% endfor %}</ul>

<h2>7 · Final cohort size</h2>
<p>Shortlisted methods were fitted on stratified probe cohorts of {{ sp.probe_sizes|join(', ') }} observations. Log-log slopes (floored at 1) projected their cost at each candidate size, with a {{ cfg.final.safety_factor|fmt }}× safety factor. The limits were: per-run timeout {{ cfg.pilot.timeout_minutes_per_run|fmt }} min, final-stage budget {{ cfg.final.time_budget_minutes|fmt }} min, memory {{ cfg.final.memory_budget_gb|fmt }} GB.</p>
<p><strong>Declared final size: {{ '{:,}'.format(sp.declared_final_size) }}</strong> of {{ '{:,}'.format(sp.available_observations) }} available observations (cap {{ '{:,}'.format(sp.configured_cap) }}); binding constraint: {{ sp.binding_constraint }}.</p>
<table><thead><tr><th>Method</th><th>Time exponent</th><th>Memory exponent</th><th>Measured at n={{ '{:,}'.format(sp.probe_sizes[-1]) }}</th><th>Projected at declared n</th></tr></thead><tbody>
{% set chosen_proj = (sp.projections|selectattr('n', 'equalto', sp.declared_final_size)|list)[0] %}
{% for m, x in sp.scaling_model.items() %}<tr><td>{{ names[m] }}</td><td>{{ '%.2f'|format(x.time_exponent) }}</td><td>{{ '%.2f'|format(x.memory_exponent) }}</td><td>{{ '%.2f'|format(x.anchor_seconds) }} s · {{ '%.0f'|format(x.anchor_memory_mb) }} MB</td><td>{{ '%.1f'|format(chosen_proj.per_method[m].seconds) }} s · {{ '%.0f'|format(chosen_proj.per_method[m].memory_mb) }} MB</td></tr>{% endfor %}
</tbody></table>
{% set f = figures['scaling'] %}<figure><img src="{{ f.path }}"><figcaption>{{ f.caption }}</figcaption></figure>

<h2>8 · Final results</h2>
<table><thead><tr><th>Method</th><th>T</th><th>R</th><th>G</th><th>T (k={{ cfg.pilot.n_neighbors_secondary }})</th><th>R (k={{ cfg.pilot.n_neighbors_secondary }})</th><th>Collapse</th><th>Silhouette (secondary)</th><th>Fit s</th></tr></thead><tbody>
{% for r in final %}<tr><td>{{ names[r.method] }}</td>{% for key in ['trustworthiness','neighbor_recall','global_structure','trustworthiness_k2','neighbor_recall_k2','collapse_ratio'] %}<td>{{ '%.3f'|format(r[key]) }}</td>{% endfor %}<td>{{ '%.3f'|format(r.silhouette) if r.silhouette is not none else '–' }}</td><td>{{ '%.2f'|format(r.runtime_seconds) }}</td></tr>{% endfor %}
</tbody></table>
<p class="small">Final metrics are in-cohort descriptions of the declared final cohort. They are not held-out estimates and should not be compared with pilot values as if the observation sets were identical. Chosen parameters: {% for m, p in chosen.items() %}{{ names[m] }} ({{ p|params }}){% if not loop.last %}; {% endif %}{% endfor %}.</p>
{% set f = figures['final_embeddings'] %}<figure><img src="{{ f.path }}"><figcaption>{{ f.caption }}</figcaption></figure>
{% set f = figures['pca_variance'] %}<figure><img src="{{ f.path }}" class="narrow"><figcaption>{{ f.caption }}</figcaption></figure>

<h2>9 · Limitations</h2>
<ul class="small">
<li>Q is one pre-registered weighting of label-free criteria. The robustness table shows which conclusions survive other reasonable weightings; no weighting establishes a universally superior method.</li>
<li>The collapse and spectral-gap checks are conservative and catch only extreme failures. A layout can still be visually degenerate above the thresholds.</li>
<li>Runtimes are single-threaded CPU measurements on one node, and material-difference tolerances absorb run-to-run noise. The size projections are conservative planning envelopes, not fitted complexity laws.</li>
<li>GPLVM uses a fixed epoch budget (loss plateau recorded), not a convergence proof.</li>
<li>PBMC annotations come from a prior clustering, and PathMNIST pixel distances need not reflect histological semantics. Class colors and silhouettes are secondary diagnostics, not validation.</li>
</ul>

<h2>10 · Reproducibility</h2>
<p class="small">Configuration SHA-256 {{ manifest.config_hash }} · code SHA-256 {{ manifest.code_hash }} · git commit {{ manifest.git_commit }} · job {{ manifest.job_id }} on {{ manifest.hostname }} · {{ manifest.created_at }}.</p>
<p class="small">Software: {% for k, v in manifest.package_versions.items() %}{{ k }} {{ v }}{% if not loop.last %} · {% endif %}{% endfor %}.</p>
<p class="small">Source: {{ profile.provenance.url|default('synthetic') }}{% if profile.provenance.license %} · license {{ profile.provenance.license }}{% endif %}{% if profile.provenance.access_date %} · accessed {{ profile.provenance.access_date }}{% endif %}. Cached file checksums: {% for k, v in (profile.provenance.files or {}).items() %}{{ k }} {{ v[:12] }}…{% if not loop.last %}; {% endif %}{% endfor %}</p>
<p class="small">References: Scanpy PBMC3k documentation and 10x Genomics PBMC3k; Yang et al., MedMNIST v2, Scientific Data 10:41 (2023); Titsias &amp; Lawrence, Bayesian GPLVM, AISTATS (2010); van der Maaten &amp; Hinton, t-SNE, JMLR (2008); McInnes et al., UMAP (2018); Coifman &amp; Lafon, Diffusion maps (2006); Venna &amp; Kaski, trustworthiness (2001). Full links: docs/METHOD_NOTES.md and docs/DATA_PROVENANCE.md.</p>
</body></html>
